window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-474523711974414a"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"usage-insights-for-chatgpt-work-in-codex\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"chatgpt-work-codex\">ChatGPT Work 与 Codex 的用量洞察</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 后添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>Admin Console 中的 Insights 可帮助你了解团队如何使用 ChatGPT Work 和 Codex，以及额度用在了哪些方面。在工作区概览中打开某个分类，即可查看其任务和用量。比较结果前，请先确认每个视图显示的统计范围。</p> <p>利用这些视图找出需要与相关负责人一起评估的工作流。将用量和支出与团队记录结合起来，了解工作是否减少了耗时、达到了质量标准或带来了更好的结果。</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iZE2r-Vx5b8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">观看：评估 ChatGPT Work 的用量与价值（需联网）</a></p> <p><a id=\"analytics-views\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">分析视图</h2> <p><a href=\"https://admin.openai.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin Console（需联网）</a>包含 ChatGPT Work 和 Codex 的分析。Usage 显示活动和消耗；Insights 将用量归入分类和任务；对于工程工作，Code review 会显示代码审查活动和发现项。</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/use-case-table.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在官网查看图片：Insights 用例表，包含分类指标（需联网）</a></p> <p>如果要查看 Token，请使用 Usage 中提供的 Token 指标。消息占比、额度占比和 Token 占比表示不同的内容；比较或分享结果时，请保留这些指标的原始名称和含义。</p> <p><a id=\"open-insights\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"insights\">打开 Insights</h2> <p>在 <a href=\"https://admin.openai.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin Console（需联网）</a>中选择你的工作区，然后打开 <strong>Analytics &gt; Insights</strong>。你需要拥有该工作区分析数据的访问权限；可见视图和数据取决于你的权限和已启用的功能。</p> <p>阅读结果之前，请确认工作区、日期范围和可用筛选条件。比较活动时要保持这些设置一致。Insights 历史数据仅从分类功能开始运行时起提供。</p> <p><a id=\"use-cases-and-tasks\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">用例与任务</h2> <p>在 Overview 中使用 <strong>Use cases / Tasks</strong> 开关，在宽泛类别和更具体的活动之间切换。在 <strong>Use cases</strong> 标签中展开一个分类，即可查看其中的任务。</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/use-cases-chart.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在官网查看图片：显示宽泛分类和示例数据的用例图表（需联网）</a></p> <p>在图表中选择一个用例或任务，即可打开详情。使用 <strong>Use cases</strong> 表格比较前 10 名以外的分类和任务。</p> <p>一个分类中可能包含多个工作流。不要把它当成单一业务流程；请先查看其中的任务。如果部分活动尚未分类，在描述结果时要注明这一限制。</p> <p><a id=\"messages-credits-and-active-users\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">消息、额度与活跃用户</h2> <p>同时查看表格中的 <strong>Messages</strong>、<strong>Credits</strong> 和 <strong>Active users</strong>，才能理解每个分类或任务。如果页面显示抽样提示，所显示的计数代表抽样活动。不要按比例放大这些数字来推算整个工作区的活动总量。</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/expanded-tasks.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在官网查看图片：Use cases 表格中展开为任务的 Software engineering 分类（需联网）</a></p> <p><strong>Messages</strong> 显示与某个分类或任务相关的消息数。消息数不能说明团队完成了多少工作。</p> <p><strong>Share of credits</strong> 显示与某个分类或任务相关的额度消耗占比。应结合 <strong>Credits</strong> 和 <strong>Messages</strong> 一起查看，了解消耗集中在哪里。</p> <p><strong>Active users</strong> 显示在某个分类或任务中活跃的人数。结合 <strong>Messages</strong> 查看，可以比较使用该分类的人数和该分类产生的活动量。</p> <p>如果某个分类占用了很大比例的额度，请检查其中的任务、模型和设置。较复杂的工作或不同的模型选择可能解释了该分类的额度消耗。在判断消耗是否值得之前，请先查看团队完成了什么。</p> <p>如果某个分类的活跃用户较少，请询问他们如何使用以及遇到了什么困难。他们可能有值得分享的工作流，也可能需要更多支持。</p> <p><a id=\"category-details\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">分类详情</h2> <p>打开某个分类的详情，即可在右侧抽屉面板中查看它的任务和用量明细。</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/category-details.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在官网查看图片：Software engineering 侧栏，显示任务、模型、推理和速度（需联网）</a></p> <p>查看该分类中的任务及各任务的额度消耗。模型、推理和速度明细会显示所选分类或任务中每个选项对应的额度占比。如果消耗量发生变化，请询问团队工作内容或这些设置是否有所改变。</p> <p>如有提供，可查看该分类或任务中的插件和技能调用情况。这些计数涵盖所选日期和筛选范围内的 ChatGPT Work 与 Codex 活动。调用次数不等同于消息数或已完成任务数。</p> <p>分享发现时，请将估算明确标记为估算值。插件和技能的额度分配可能有重叠，因此不要把这两个视图相加来计算总投入。有关额度和账单影响的更多信息，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-ba100f6664b7be87\">ChatGPT Work：用量与成本</a>。</p> <h2 id=\"code-review\">Code review</h2> <p>如果你要评估工程工作，请打开 <strong>Code review</strong>，查看工作区可用的代码审查指标。</p> <ul> <li><strong>PRs reviewed</strong> 显示拉取请求审查活动。拉取请求经过审查，并不意味着它一定已合并或部署。</li> <li><strong>Issues found</strong> 显示这些审查发现的问题。请与审查人员确认哪些发现有用，以及哪些问题已采取行动。</li> <li><strong>Issues by priority, reactions, and reaction sentiment</strong> 为发现的问题及用户的响应提供更多背景信息。</li> </ul> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/code-review-prs-reviewed.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在官网查看图片：显示示例拉取请求审查活动的 PRs reviewed 图表（需联网）</a></p> <p>计数为零，可能表示没有活动，也可能是报告存在缺口。解读该数值之前，请确认日期范围及相关审查是否包含在内。</p> <p><a id=\"assessing-value\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">评估价值</h2> <p>选择团队在 ChatGPT Work 或 Codex 中使用的一项工作流。与业务负责人商定要改善的结果以及衡量方法。将 Insights 与团队记录（例如客户资料简报、库存计划或拉取请求）结合查看。评估时应让实际执行工作的人参与。</p> <p>使用一致的报告期间，并留意任何抽样提示。分类中可能包含多个工作流，活动计数并不等于已完成工作量。以下示例展示如何结合用量数据和工作流证据评估价值。</p> <p><a id=\"fixing-bugs\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">修复错误</h3> <p>Codex 是否帮助工程师减少调查和返工，更快地修复错误？</p> <p>选择某个服务中的一类重复错误，例如输入处理不正确。请熟悉相关代码的工程师一起审查问题、修复方案和回归测试。</p> <p><strong>调查方法</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>比较相似的修复工作。</strong> 记录复杂度相近的错误在调查、实现和审查方面所花的时间。将实际投入时间与等待审查或发布的时间区分开。</li> <li><strong>查看 Insights。</strong> 打开 Software engineering，查找与调查相关的任务。查看比较期间的额度和活跃用户。</li> <li><strong>确认结果。</strong> 检查测试是否能复现错误，以及修复后是否通过。询问工程师作了哪些修正，并记录重新打开的问题或回归错误。</li> <li><strong>如果确认修复所需的总投入更少，就分享该工作流。</strong> 如果返工仍然很多，请改进复现步骤或代码仓库上下文，再次比较。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"adding-tests\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">添加测试</h3> <p>Codex 是否帮助团队以更少的人工投入覆盖重要故障情况？</p> <p>选择一个已知测试覆盖缺口的模块。比较结果之前，应先明确哪些行为和故障情况需要测试。</p> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/category-details.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在官网查看图片：分类详情，其中包含任务和模型、推理、速度明细（需联网）</a></p> <p><strong>调查方法</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>定义缺口。</strong> 列出缺少测试的行为，并记录新增类似测试所需的投入。使用测试报告记录当前覆盖率。</li> <li><strong>查看 Insights。</strong> 在 Software engineering 下查找相关任务，查看同一期间的额度，以及可用的模型和推理明细。</li> <li><strong>检查测试。</strong> 请工程师确认断言能捕获预期的故障。记录不稳定的测试、增加的运行时间，以及重写或维护测试花费的时间。</li> <li><strong>如果有用的测试更容易完成，就复用这种做法。</strong> 如果测试通过了却没有捕获故障，请明确预期行为后再试。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"refactoring-code\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">重构代码</h3> <p>Codex 是否帮助团队在保持预期行为的同时完成重构？</p> <p>选择一项范围明确的更改，例如在某个软件包中替换已弃用的 API。明确要修改哪些调用位置，以及团队如何验证结果。</p> <p><strong>调查方法</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>确定范围。</strong> 记录要更新的调用位置，并估算手动完成类似更改所需的投入。对于此前一直延期的工作，要明确标记估算值。</li> <li><strong>查看 Insights。</strong> 检查相关 Software engineering 任务和额度。如果消耗显著，请查看可用的模型和推理明细。</li> <li><strong>验证更改。</strong> 审查差异、运行相关检查，并查找遗漏的调用位置或行为变化。将审查、修正和后续修复所需的时间计入总投入。</li> <li><strong>如果重构满足约定的检查标准，再扩展到另一个软件包。</strong> 如果仍有太多清理工作，请缩小范围或先提供一个可运行的示例。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"account-research\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">客户资料调研</h3> <p>ChatGPT Work 是否帮助销售人员以更少的时间准备准确的客户简报？</p> <p>选择一个定期准备简报的销售团队。商定每份简报应包含哪些内容，例如客户历史、当前重点和需要向客户了解的问题。</p> <p><strong>调查方法</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>比较相似的简报。</strong> 记录试点前后准备和审查所需的时间。使用相同的质量标准，并选择调研需求相近的客户账户。</li> <li><strong>查看 Insights。</strong> 在 Sales 下查找客户调研和计划任务。使用可用的群组筛选器聚焦目标团队，并查看同一期间的额度、模型选择，以及可用的插件或技能活动。</li> <li><strong>与销售人员一起审查简报。</strong> 根据源记录核实事实，并评估调研是否有助于准备客户沟通。将修正所需时间计入投入，并跟踪节省的时间是否用于客户沟通或后续工作。</li> <li><strong>如果准确简报所需投入更少，就分享该做法。</strong> 如果缺少重要上下文，请改进源材料或提供共享技能。后续如需评估合格商机或销售额变化，应使用 CRM 记录；Insights 本身无法证明这种联系。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"inventory-planning\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">库存计划</h3> <p>ChatGPT Work 是否帮助团队以更少的人工投入制定可靠的库存计划？</p> <p>选择一个定期规划周期，例如活动所需库存。明确涉及哪些产品和地点，以及团队将使用哪些销售和库存记录。</p> <p><strong>调查方法</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>记录当前流程。</strong> 衡量收集记录、准备计划和修正内容所花的时间。记录类似周期中的缺货或库存过剩情况。</li> <li><strong>查看 Insights。</strong> 查找与团队计划工作匹配的分类和任务。查看同一期间的额度和活跃用户。在将分类用量归因于该工作流之前，先与团队确认匹配情况。</li> <li><strong>将计划与实际结果对照。</strong> 请库存负责人核实数量、假设和缺失数据。将审查和修正所需时间计入投入。周期结束后，将计划库存与销量及剩余库存进行比较。</li> <li><strong>如果计划可靠且所需投入更少，就复用该工作流。</strong> 如果缺货或库存过剩增加，请重新检查输入数据和假设。评估成本是否降低时，应使用库存和采购记录。</li> </ol> <p><strong>记录评估结果。</strong> 记下用例、负责人和报告期间。包括基准、结果、额度和限制。记录商定的更改及复查日期。已完成的工作量应以团队记录为准，并将估算明确标记为估算。</p> <p>评估投资回报率（ROI）时，应将改善带来的价值与 AI、设置、培训和持续支持成本进行比较。将审查和修正工作花费的时间也计算在内。节省时间不自动等于节省现金；请检查团队如何使用节省出的产能。</p> <p>提高用量上限之前，请先检查当前上限、消耗量以及真正需要更多容量的工作。已消耗额度不一定会成为额外账单费用。请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-ba100f6664b7be87\">ChatGPT Work：用量与成本</a>。</p> <p>用量洞察只是理解 ChatGPT Work 和 Codex 投资回报的一部分。它显示所选范围内的用量和额度消耗。实际执行工作的团队可以解释发生了哪些变化、结果是否有所改善，以及改善的价值。结合这两类信息，决定要扩展哪些工作流，以及团队在哪些方面需要更多支持。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"usage-insights-for-chatgpt-work-in-codex\">Usage Insights for ChatGPT Work in Codex</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Insights in the Admin Console helps you understand what teams use ChatGPT Work and Codex for and where credits are spent. Open a category in the workspace overview to see its tasks and usage. Check the scope shown in each view before comparing results.</p> <p>Use these views to identify workflows to assess with the people responsible for them. Pair usage and spend with team records to understand whether the work takes less effort, meets quality standards, or produces better results.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iZE2r-Vx5b8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Watch: Assess Usage and Value of ChatGPT Work (online)</a></p> <h2 id=\"analytics-views\">Analytics views</h2> <p>The <a href=\"https://admin.openai.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin Console (online)</a> includes analytics for ChatGPT Work and Codex. Usage shows activity and consumption. Insights groups usage into categories and tasks. For engineering work, Code review shows review activity and findings.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Insights Use cases table with category metrics · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/use-case-table.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Insights Use cases table with category metrics · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/use-case-table.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>If you're looking at tokens, use the token measures available in Usage. Message share, credit share, and token share describe different things; keep those labels intact when comparing or sharing a result.</p> <h2 id=\"open-insights\">Open Insights</h2> <p>In the <a href=\"https://admin.openai.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin Console (online)</a>, select your workspace and open <strong>Analytics &gt; Insights</strong>. You'll need access to the analytics for that workspace; the views and data you see depend on your permissions and enabled features.</p> <p>Check the workspace, date range, and available filters before reading the results. Keep them consistent when comparing activity. Insights history is available only from when classification began.</p> <h2 id=\"use-cases-and-tasks\">Use cases and tasks</h2> <p>On Overview, use the Use cases / Tasks toggle to switch between broad categories and more specific activity. In the Use cases tab, expand a category to see its tasks.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Use cases chart showing broad categories with sample data · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/use-cases-chart.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Use cases chart showing broad categories with sample data · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/use-cases-chart.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>Select a use case or task in the chart to open its details. Use the Use cases table to compare categories and tasks beyond the top 10.</p> <p>A category may include several workflows. Check its tasks before treating it as a single business process. If some activity is unclassified, note that limitation when describing the results.</p> <h2 id=\"messages-credits-and-active-users\">Messages, credits, and active users</h2> <p>Read the table's Messages, Credits, and Active users together to understand each category or task. If a sampling notice appears, the counts shown reflect sampled activity. Don't scale them up to estimate total workspace activity.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Software engineering expanded into tasks in the Use cases table · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/expanded-tasks.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Software engineering expanded into tasks in the Use cases table · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/expanded-tasks.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><strong>Messages</strong> shows the number of messages associated with a category or task. A message count doesn't tell you how much work the team finished.</p> <p><strong>Share of credits</strong> shows the portion of credit consumption associated with a category or task. Read it alongside Credits and Messages to understand where consumption is concentrated.</p> <p><strong>Active users</strong> shows the number of people active in a category or task. Read it alongside Messages to compare how many people use a category with how much activity it generates.</p> <p>If a category accounts for a large share of credits, check its tasks, models, and settings. More complex work or different model choices may explain the category's credit use. Review what the team accomplished before deciding whether that consumption is worthwhile.</p> <p>If a category has few active users, ask them how they're using it and where they're having difficulty. They may have a workflow worth sharing or need more support.</p> <h2 id=\"category-details\">Category details</h2> <p>Open a category's details to see its tasks and usage breakdowns in a drawer on the right.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Software engineering drawer showing tasks, models, reasoning, and speed · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/category-details.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Software engineering drawer showing tasks, models, reasoning, and speed · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/category-details.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>Review the tasks in the category and the credits used by each one. The model, reasoning, and speed breakdowns show each option's share of credits within the selected category or task. If consumption changes, ask the team whether the work or these settings changed.</p> <p>Where available, review plugin and skill invocations for the category or task. These counts include activity across ChatGPT Work and Codex within the selected dates and filters. Invocations aren't the same as messages or completed tasks.</p> <p>Keep estimates labeled as estimates when you share a finding. Plugin and skill credit allocations can overlap, so don't add those views together to calculate total investment. For more on interpreting credits and billing impact, see <a href=\"#/article/a-ba100f6664b7be87\">ChatGPT Work usage and cost</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"code-review\">Code review</h2> <p>If you're reviewing engineering work, open <strong>Code review</strong> to see the review measures available to your workspace.</p> <ul> <li><strong>PRs reviewed</strong> shows pull-request review activity. A reviewed pull request isn't necessarily merged or deployed.</li> <li><strong>Issues found</strong> shows findings from those reviews. Check with reviewers to understand which findings were useful and acted on.</li> <li><strong>Issues by priority, reactions, and reaction sentiment</strong> add context about the findings and how people responded.</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">PRs reviewed chart showing sample pull-request review activity · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/code-review-prs-reviewed.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>PRs reviewed chart showing sample pull-request review activity · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/code-review-prs-reviewed.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>A zero count can reflect no activity or a gap in reporting. Check the date range and whether the relevant reviews are included before interpreting the count.</p> <h2 id=\"assessing-value\">Assessing value</h2> <p>Choose a workflow your team uses in ChatGPT Work or Codex. Agree with the business owner on the result to improve and how you'll measure it. Review Insights alongside team records, such as account briefs, inventory plans, or pull requests. Include the people doing the work in the assessment.</p> <p>Use a consistent reporting period and check any sampling notice. Categories can include several workflows, and activity counts don't measure completed work. The examples below show how to investigate value using both usage data and evidence from the workflow.</p> <h3 id=\"fixing-bugs\">Fixing bugs</h3> <p>Is Codex helping engineers resolve bugs with less investigation and rework?</p> <p>Choose a recurring bug type in one service, such as incorrect input handling. Review the issues, fixes, and regression tests with an engineer who knows that code.</p> <p><strong>How to investigate</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Compare similar fixes.</strong> Record investigation, implementation, and review time for bugs of similar complexity. Separate hands-on effort from time waiting for a review or release.</li> <li><strong>Check Insights.</strong> Open Software engineering and look for tasks relevant to the investigation. Review credits and active users for the period you're comparing.</li> <li><strong>Confirm the result.</strong> Check that the test reproduces the bug and passes with the fix. Ask what engineers corrected, and note reopened issues or regressions.</li> <li><strong>If confirmed fixes need less total effort, share the workflow.</strong> If rework stays high, improve the reproduction steps or repository context and compare again.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"adding-tests\">Adding tests</h3> <p>Is Codex helping the team cover important failure cases with less manual effort?</p> <p>Choose a module with a known coverage gap. Agree which behaviors and failure cases need tests before comparing the results.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Category details with tasks and model, reasoning, and speed breakdowns · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/category-details.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Category details with tasks and model, reasoning, and speed breakdowns · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-codex-analytics/category-details.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><strong>How to investigate</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Define the gap.</strong> List the missing behaviors and record the effort needed to add comparable tests. Use your test reports to capture the starting coverage.</li> <li><strong>Check Insights.</strong> Find relevant tasks under Software engineering. Review credits and the available model and reasoning breakdowns for the same period.</li> <li><strong>Inspect the tests.</strong> Have an engineer check that assertions catch the intended failures. Note flaky results, added runtime, and time spent rewriting or maintaining the tests.</li> <li><strong>Reuse the approach if useful tests take less effort to land.</strong> If they pass without catching the failure, clarify the expected behavior and try again.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"refactoring-code\">Refactoring code</h3> <p>Is Codex helping the team finish a refactor while preserving expected behavior?</p> <p>Choose one bounded change, such as replacing a deprecated API across a package. Agree which call sites are in scope and how the team will verify the result.</p> <p><strong>How to investigate</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Set the scope.</strong> Record the call sites to update and the effort for a comparable manual change. Label estimates, especially if the work was previously deferred.</li> <li><strong>Check Insights.</strong> Review relevant Software engineering tasks and their credits for the same period. Check the available model and reasoning breakdowns if consumption stands out.</li> <li><strong>Validate the change.</strong> Review the diff, run the relevant checks, and look for missed call sites or behavior changes. Include review, corrections, and follow-up fixes in the effort.</li> <li><strong>Expand to another package if the refactor meets the agreed checks.</strong> If too much cleanup remains, narrow the change or provide a working example first.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"account-research\">Account research</h3> <p>Is ChatGPT Work helping sellers prepare accurate account briefs with less effort?</p> <p>Choose a sales team that prepares briefs regularly. Agree what each brief should include, such as account history, current priorities, and questions for the customer.</p> <p><strong>How to investigate</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Compare similar briefs.</strong> Record preparation and review time before and during the trial. Use the same quality criteria and accounts that need a similar level of research.</li> <li><strong>Check Insights.</strong> Look for account research and planning under Sales. Use the available group filter to focus on the team. Review credits, model choices, and any available plugin or skill activity for the same period.</li> <li><strong>Review the briefs with sellers.</strong> Check the facts against source records and assess whether the research helps prepare for the conversation. Include corrections in the effort, and track whether time saved goes into customer conversations or follow-up.</li> <li><strong>Share the approach if accurate briefs take less effort.</strong> If important context is missing, improve the source material or provide a shared skill. Use CRM records to assess any later change in qualified opportunities or sales; Insights alone doesn't establish that connection.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"inventory-planning\">Inventory planning</h3> <p>Is ChatGPT Work helping the team prepare reliable inventory plans with less manual work?</p> <p>Choose a recurring planning cycle, such as stock for an event. Agree which products and locations are in scope and which sales and stock records the team will use.</p> <p><strong>How to investigate</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Record the current process.</strong> Measure time spent gathering records, preparing the plan, and correcting it. Note stock shortages or excess stock from comparable cycles.</li> <li><strong>Check Insights.</strong> Find the category and tasks that match the team's planning work. Review credits and active users for the same period. Confirm the match with the team before attributing the category's usage to this workflow.</li> <li><strong>Check the plan against actual results.</strong> Have the inventory owner verify quantities, assumptions, and missing data. Include review and corrections in the effort. After the cycle, compare planned stock with sales and remaining inventory.</li> <li><strong>Reuse the workflow if plans are reliable and take less effort.</strong> If stock shortages or excess stock increase, revisit the inputs and assumptions. Use inventory and purchasing records to assess any cost reduction.</li> </ol> <p><strong>Record the assessment.</strong> Note the use case, owner, and reporting period. Include the baseline, results, credits, and limitations. Record any changes agreed with the team and a date to review them. Count completed work from team records, and label estimates.</p> <p>To assess ROI, compare the value of the improvement with the costs of AI, setup, training, and ongoing support. Include time spent reviewing and correcting the work. Time saved isn't automatically a cash saving; check how the team uses that capacity.</p> <p>Before raising usage limits, review current limits, consumption, and the work that needs more capacity. Credits consumed aren't automatically an additional invoice charge. See <a href=\"#/article/a-ba100f6664b7be87\">ChatGPT Work usage and cost</a>.</p> <p>Usage insights are one part of understanding the return on your investment in ChatGPT Work and Codex. They show usage and credit consumption within the selected scope. The teams doing the work can explain what changed, whether results improved, and what that improvement is worth. Use both to decide which workflows to expand and where the team needs more support.</p>"};
